1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
It's Mommy.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,680
Why does she seem so different?

3
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:15,160
Her magic feels scary.

4
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:20,420
Tsuruna?

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,500
Thank goodness!

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:22,160
Not even.

7
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:25,200
She's got other stuff on her mind besides talking.

8
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,200
Yeah, but...

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,380
Toka, we started the Magius because we wanted to save magical girls, but all we're doing

10
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:43,800
now is hurting them.

11
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,340
What's gotten into you, Nemu?

12
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,500
We have to become gods if we're gonna save magical girls.

13
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:51,120
That's the whole point of all this.

14
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,080
You know that.

15
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:31,500
Welcome to Kelation Land! Have fuuuuun!

16
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:35,500
It's me, Tsuruno! Hiroha! Hiroha Tamaki!

17
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,500
Someone's controlling her mind.

18
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,500
We'll save you.

19
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:42,500
We'll save all magical girls.

20
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:50,500
Mami Tomoe the Badass ends up as someone's puppet. Damn, that's pathetic. It's almost funny.

21
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:54,500
Chiro finale. Holy night.

22
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,500
That got her going!

23
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,500
Tommy, now she's pissed!

24
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,500
Pumura! On it!

25
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,500
Any time now, Pumura!

26
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,500
My time stops malfunctioning!

27
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,500
This area's not like a witch's labyrinth.

28
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,500
It's part of the enemy!

29
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:36,500
You should take it easy! Just relax and have fun!

30
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:41,500
You don't have to work so hard anymore!

31
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,500
Stop your hurt, Tsuruno!

32
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,500
Come on, Tsuruno!

33
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,500
Come on, Tsuruno! Wake up!

34
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:50,500
Remember who you are!

35
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,500
Yachiyo!

36
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:01,500
Touka and Namu, do you see what's happening here?

37
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,500
I can't believe you're okay with this!

38
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:07,500
I just wanna talk, so please come out and talk to me!

39
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:11,500
Try to keep your voice down. Don't disturb the other guests!

40
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,500
Phew! That was too close!

41
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:23,500
Sana! Felicia!

42
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,500
Hurry! Let's connect!

43
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,500
Time to wake up!

44
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,500
Wake up! Tsuruno!

45
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:40,500
W-what the heck?

46
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,500
Let's get going while the getting's good!

47
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:55,500
The largest supercell on record is heading north and is growing even stronger.

48
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:59,500
It is predicted to reach the mainland in about six hours.

49
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,500
We only have six hours left!

50
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:17,500
I'm so happy the two of you are okay!

51
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:20,500
Not as happy as us! We were worried about you!

52
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:25,500
Speak for yourself, Sana! I told you Iroha's indestructible! Just like...

53
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:27,500
Hiyachiyo...

54
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,500
W-what's up?

55
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:34,500
He disappeared without saying anything to me.

56
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:37,500
Do you have any idea how worried I was?

57
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,500
Sorry about that...

58
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:44,500
Don't go running off again without at least leaving a note.

59
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:47,500
Now you know how ruthless the Magias are.

60
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,500
And how dangerous.

61
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,500
I do.

62
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,500
What is it?

63
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:58,500
When I joined them, it was cause the Magias said they'd save us.

64
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:01,500
But their plan sucks and now they got everyone brainwashed.

65
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,500
Even Tsuruno too.

66
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,500
I'll figure out how to get Tsuruno back to us.

67
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:10,500
As for becoming a witch, I won't ever let that happen to you.

68
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,500
Even if it costs me my life.

69
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:13,500
Don't worry.

70
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,500
No, you don't get it.

71
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:15,500
Of course I do.

72
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,500
You're scared, but I'll protect you no matter what.

73
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,500
Geez, do I have to spell it out for you?

74
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:21,500
Yes, maybe you should.

75
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:25,500
If you didn't use your doppel when you did, you'd have turned into a witch by now.

76
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,500
I don't want that to happen to you.

77
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:30,500
I want you to stay-

78
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:35,500
The fate of all Magical Girls is the price we pay for the wish we were granted.

79
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:40,500
And I will not force others to succumb to their fate so that I can delay mine.

80
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:41,500
I want no part of that.

81
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,500
So we're screwed either way?

82
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:45,500
First you said you'd keep me from turning a witch.

83
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,500
That's way different than what you just said!

84
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:48,500
Calm down.

85
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:54,500
The point I'm trying to make is that you have to get strong enough so you don't need to rely on your doppel.

86
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,500
And while I'm still around-

87
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,500
What are you saying?!

88
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,500
That can't happen to you!

89
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,500
I don't want it to!

90
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:04,500
That's my problem, and I'll deal with it.

91
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,500
I'll forget I said anything!

92
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,500
Felicia, wait!

93
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:09,500
Leave me alone, you big fat jerk!

94
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,500
Felicia!

95
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,500
Well, that was something.

96
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:18,500
How-

97
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:22,500
You could've picked a better time to drop that bomb on her.

98
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,500
I hate lies.

99
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,500
If you say so.

100
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,500
Here, take one.

101
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,500
Right now, really?

102
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:34,500
Girl, there's no better time than now.

103
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,500
I'd like to have one!

104
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,500
Iroha...

105
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,500
May I have one too?

106
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,500
Mmm!

107
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,500
Hey Iroha...

108
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:51,500
Is that Tsuruno girl a friend of yours?

109
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:52,500
Yep.

110
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,500
One of my best friends, actually.

111
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:56,500
She lives with us at Mikazuki Villa.

112
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:58,500
That's nice.

113
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:02,500
Is Mami Tomoe a good friend of yours?

114
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:03,500
Uh-huh.

115
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:08,500
She's a veteran magical girl, and she taught us how to use our powers and stuff.

116
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:10,500
So why is she fighting us?

117
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:12,500
The Magius got in her head.

118
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,500
Wait!

119
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,500
Do you know something about it?

120
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:19,500
When I was sneaking around in Fent Hope, I saw some things.

121
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:26,500
They were putting this weird crap into soul gems, and I heard one of them say it was to give magic powers a boost.

122
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:31,500
I also heard something about fusing Uwasa and magical girls. Bet they finished that job by now.

123
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:35,500
That's horrible! Do you know if what they're doing can be undone?

124
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:38,500
How should I know? I just heard them talk about it.

125
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:42,500
Oh, wait a sec. We saw Mifuyu on the way out. She gave us this.

126
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,500
Did she now?

127
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:57,500
Look at that. It's a map of Chelation Land.

128
00:08:57,500 --> 00:09:01,500
It says here, Operation Awaken Embryo Eve.

129
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,500
That Eve thingy! Touka mentioned it!

130
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:08,500
With this, we have the details of the Magius' plan.

131
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:16,500
She betrayed them.

132
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:21,500
Before she gave me that, Mifuyu said she'd bring Sudono back to us.

133
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:26,500
That's Chelation Castle, alright. Hotel Fent Hope's right under it.

134
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:29,500
Look it! That's where Mommy and the others came out.

135
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:37,500
If what this note says is true, and I believe it is, there's an Uwasa station there, which acts as a kind of beacon to attract the witches.

136
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,500
Getting there won't be easy.

137
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:42,500
Excuse me. I was wondering about that beacon thing.

138
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:44,500
Why do they want witches to come here?

139
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:50,500
Because the Magius think that by drawing all the witches here, they'll lure Valpurgisnacht here too.

140
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:58,500
And according to this, they made an artificial witch named Embryo Eve to absorb Valpurgisnacht.

141
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:01,500
That Embryo Eve thing's real. I totally saw it.

142
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:06,500
It's like the biggest witch ever and they were feeding it train cars full of witches.

143
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:10,500
I saw it too. It was awful.

144
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:16,500
I guess what those Magius dorks think is if it eats Valpurgisnacht, it'll free us magical girls somehow.

145
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:25,500
Honestly, I don't care what the Magius think. Their plan's insane and we have to stop it. And to do that, we have to destroy that beacon.

146
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:31,500
Okay, but what about Tsuruno and Mami? They'll try to stop us.

147
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,500
You're right. We should save them first.

148
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:37,500
We just have to figure out how we're gonna break this spell they're under.

149
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:43,500
I have an idea about that.

150
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:45,500
You're kidding. Mifuyu?

151
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:50,500
I'm sorry, Yachun. I hoped I could free Tsuruno by now, but I'm still trying.

152
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:53,500
You expect me to trust you after everything?

153
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:57,500
No, I don't. But believe me, I feel horrible about it.

154
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,500
Well, it's too late for that.

155
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:07,500
I know. I was stupid. But now I want to make things right. I'm on my way to see someone who might be able to help.

156
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:19,500
Isn't there anything you can do to turn them back?

157
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:25,500
I told you before, if the Magius' plan works, then might do it. Maybe, maybe not. I don't know.

158
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,500
I can't believe the best chance they have is a maybe.

159
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:39,500
A doppel is the incarnation of the darkness in a magical girl's heart.

160
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:43,500
If I so much as touch it, it would absorb me, so there's nothing I can do.

161
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:47,500
Actually, there is something you can do for me.

162
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,500
M-Mifuyu...

163
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:57,500
Mitama, if you know of a way to turn Tsuruno and Mami back to normal, I need you to tell me.

164
00:11:57,500 --> 00:12:00,500
You're asking the impossible.

165
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:05,500
I can't risk my reputation. My business is based on my client's trust in me.

166
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:08,500
I'm obliged to remain confidential and neutral.

167
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:12,500
For just this once, could you drop the neutrality talk?

168
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:15,500
Wait, what happened? Is Tsuruno okay?

169
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:18,500
No, she's not.

170
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,500
She's been fused with the Nuasa.

171
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:25,500
Huh?

172
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,500
Coordinator, you have to help her.

173
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:31,500
I'll pay you in cash, grief seats, whatever.

174
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,500
You have to save Tsuruno, please!

175
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:39,500
You don't even know why she is the way she is, so I'm sorry, but I can't get involved.

176
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:44,500
Who cares about why or whatever? She's my friend and I can't leave her like that!

177
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:48,500
I'm sorry. It's not my problem, so I can't get involved.

178
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:51,500
I can't believe you.

179
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:56,500
You're using your neutrality as an excuse to ignore something you're part of!

180
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:58,500
Am I now?

181
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,500
Am I now?

182
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:06,500
How dare you? You don't know anything about me, do you?

183
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:11,500
You don't know me at all, so watch what you say to me.

184
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:15,500
No. No, I don't.

185
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,500
What difference does that make?

186
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:22,500
I don't know you, or Kaede, or Tsuruno, or even Yachiyo!

187
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:24,500
There, I admit it!

188
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:29,500
I just pretended I did, so I didn't have to face what was really going on!

189
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:36,500
I didn't want to know. I was scared.

190
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,500
That makes two of us, then.

191
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:48,500
The truth is, I always wanted to be a magical girl.

192
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:53,500
I thought I'd be using my magic to do good things for people.

193
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,500
I wanted to be a beacon of hope and justice.

194
00:13:56,500 --> 00:14:00,500
But things didn't work out that way in the end.

195
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:02,500
You're right.

196
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:05,500
In exchange for our wishes, we have to fight witches forever.

197
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:09,500
Until the day comes when we turn into witches.

198
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,500
I can't fight them, though.

199
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:17,500
I can work on soul gems, but that's the only magical power I have.

200
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:22,500
If I had to fight a witch, I'd either be killed, or I'd turn into one.

201
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:31,500
Since I couldn't fight, I decided to spend my days as a coordinator, that way I could earn grief seeds.

202
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:36,500
I've seen so much despair over the years.

203
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:43,500
Girls who were bright and cheerful on the outside, but in their hearts, there was so much darkness, I couldn't help them.

204
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:47,500
Some turned into witches as I tried to help them.

205
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:51,500
When I work on a soul gem, I close myself off.

206
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:55,500
That way, the darkness in my patient's heart can't infect mine.

207
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,500
I pretend I don't see it.

208
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:03,500
It's the only way for me to keep their despair from crushing me.

209
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,500
I'm so sorry.

210
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:18,500
I'm tired and afraid, afraid of touching others and getting to know them.

211
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:30,500
I get it, but you're not alone.

212
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:35,500
You suffered, and I didn't see it. I didn't want to.

213
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:41,500
If you want, I'd like to be your friend.

214
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,500
It's too late.

215
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:46,500
Stop it. Nothing's too late. Talk to me.

216
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:49,500
You don't have to go it alone. I'm here for you.

217
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,500
Okay, Momoko, you win.

218
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:57,500
But you lost your discount. I charge all my friends triple.

219
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:59,500
Why? That's discrimination!

220
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:06,500
To free Tsuruno, you'll have to attack and connect with her.

221
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:08,500
At the same time?

222
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:13,500
Yes, the Uasa doesn't belong with her, so you have to synchronize your attack with her soul.

223
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,500
That should separate the Uasa from her.

224
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:18,500
Huh?

225
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:22,500
When you attack, make sure you have a clear image of Tsuruno in your mind.

226
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,500
Then connect with her through that image.

227
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:32,500
But be careful. If your image of her is wrong in any way, it won't hurt the Uasa. It'll hurt Tsuruno.

228
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,500
Alright, thank you.

229
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:37,500
Yachiyo, that's how you'll free her.

230
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:41,500
The same tactic should work for your friend, Mami, too.

231
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,500
Thank you for helping!

232
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,500
Yes, thank you. I owe you one.

233
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:53,500
Don't worry. In fact, you don't have to pay my expenses anymore. Momoko has graciously offered to pay them. Isn't that sweet?

234
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:58,500
Hey! I didn't offer anything! Go save Tsuruno. Good luck.

235
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:03,500
This is great! Let's go get her! Then we can all go home together.

236
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,500
Right.

237
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:10,500
Before we do anything, we need to get a good image of Tsuruno in our heads to connect.

238
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:15,500
Don't worry about that. I've already got it. I know her better than anyone, after all.

239
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:18,500
I know Mami the best out of us, so I'll take care of her.

240
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:20,500
I didn't know you were tight.

241
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:22,500
I'll help however I can.

242
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:26,500
Hey, um, can I ask something?

243
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,500
Of course! What do you want to know?

244
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:31,500
What's this connect thing we have to do?

245
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,500
Wait, you don't know about that?

246
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:34,500
I don't know about that!

247
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,500
Sorry, Rena. You should move back.

248
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,500
You said working on them is dangerous!

249
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,500
That's true. It's quite dangerous.

250
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,500
However...

251
00:17:55,500 --> 00:18:02,500
This is what I wanted. To be a magical girl who helps others!

252
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:08,500
There she is!

253
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:13,500
I can't get away. I'm not fast enough.

254
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:15,500
Iroha, what do I do?

255
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,500
Do you expect me to help you?

256
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:22,500
Even though you abandoned me?

257
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:23,500
Over there!

258
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:30,500
I didn't abandon you! I couldn't! I can't!

259
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:42,500
So, just to get this straight, connecting means combining our powers like how Mami syncs her magic with us?

260
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:46,500
Yeah, but every time she did, she had to match her power with ours.

261
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:50,500
Don't worry. We can adjust our power to match Mami's easy.

262
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:57,500
Yeah, you're right. We've seen how kind and awesome she is. We know her better than anyone.

263
00:18:58,500 --> 00:18:59,500
Yeah.

264
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:01,500
Yeah.

265
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:05,500
We're gonna break our friends out of their spell.

266
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:08,500
And then, I'm gonna go find Touka and Nemu!

267
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:22,500
Whatever you do, don't hesitate! She'll unload on you for sure!

268
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:31,500
I can summon just as many!

269
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,500
I can summon just as many!

270
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:39,500
Hm…

271
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:57,680
Sada's gonna stick close to me, and we'll distract Mami for you.

272
00:19:57,680 --> 00:20:01,980
As soon as I see an opening, I'll attack in sync with Mami's magic.

273
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:08,560
Welcome to Chelation Land! The place to go for people who've given up trying!

274
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:12,740
Stop talking nonsense! You were the magical girl who always worked the hardest!

275
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:14,980
You were stronger than any of us!

276
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:20,800
Ira!

277
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:28,880
Sorry, Juno!

278
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,100
Catch you!

279
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:38,280
You always did your best. You were always cheerful.

280
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:40,220
You were stronger than anyone.

281
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:44,860
I don't know how you got like this, but I'm going to save you from it!

282
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:54,900
You're up, Sayaka!

283
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,240
Leave it to me!

284
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:02,280
Kadek!

285
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:10,160
Come on, Juno! Change back to the way you were before!

286
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:10,200
Come on, Juno! Change back to the way you were before!

287
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:10,820
Manuka!

288
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:23,460
Manuka!

289
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,960
What...what happened?

290
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:41,940
It didn't work.

291
00:21:42,660 --> 00:21:43,840
Did we do something wrong?

292
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,900
Tsuruno is the strongest.

293
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:50,320
She's stronger than everyone.

294
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,680
And since she's so strong, she's okay.

295
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:56,660
Tsuruno, stop.

296
00:21:56,660 --> 00:22:00,660
I am the strongest.

